      "content": "that \"Pattern of Operational Shifts\" idea is actually really smart. it makes it sound so much more professional.\n\nit's just so frustrating because I know exactly why they're doing this. it's like they're trying to create this constant low-level stress so I'll eventually just snap or quit without a severance package. it's a very calculated move to keep everything just under the radar of official misconduct. \n\ndo you think there's any way to find evidence that these decisions (like the meeting time or the payroll delay) were actually made by the same specific people in HR? if I can link the \"glitches\" to specific individuals, it would prove it's a targeted campaign rather than just corporate incompetence.",
